WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.842
Rain is where groundwater comes from, so MyWell
brings the weather in beside your readings.

2
00:00:05.962 --> 00:00:09.154
This tutorial is a quick look at the Weather
page.

3
00:00:09.983 --> 00:00:12.287
Now we're on: Weather.

4
00:00:12.407 --> 00:00:15.191
Before a field visit, check the sky.

5
00:00:15.311 --> 00:00:20.183
This page shows live conditions for any place,
a seven-day outlook,

6
00:00:20.303 --> 00:00:23.471
and what the week's rain means for irrigation.

7
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:26.107
Set your location.

8
00:00:26.227 --> 00:00:28.771
The forecast follows a location.

9
00:00:28.891 --> 00:00:34.651
Use your current GPS position, search for a
place, or type exact coordinates —

10
00:00:34.771 --> 00:00:38.467
handy for checking the weather at a station
before you visit.

11
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:41.059
How much to water.

12
00:00:41.179 --> 00:00:47.371
For farmers, this sums up the week: how much
water crops need, how much rain is expected,

13
00:00:47.491 --> 00:00:50.563
and the shortfall to make up by irrigating.

14
00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.459
Tap the ?

15
00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:54.571
for how it's worked out.

16
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:57.159
The week ahead.

17
00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:01.119
A seven-day outlook with temperatures and
expected rainfall —

18
00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:05.655
compare the forecast rain here with what your
rain gauge actually catches.

19
00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:08.427
That is the whole page.

20
00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:13.203
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

21
00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:16.299
Thanks for helping look after our groundwater.
